<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>Lesson Summary</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00396</md:content-id>
    <md:title>Lesson Summary</md:title>
    <md:uuid>4d6e73dc-12c1-4406-b0ff-b691777a1e04</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section id="sect-00001">
      <para id="para-00001">In this lesson, you learned how to:</para>
      <list id="list-00001">
        <item>Write a system of equations from tables of values and graphs.</item>
        <item>Graph systems of equations by hand.</item>
        <item>Estimate real-world solutions by graphing systems of equations.</item>
      </list>
      <para id="para-00002">Here are the <emphasis>activities</emphasis> that helped you reach those goals:</para>
      <list id="list-00002">
        <item>2.2.1: Interpreting Graphs of Systems of Equations
        <list id="list-00003">
          <item>In this activity, you looked at a graph of a system of equations and thought about
            what you noticed and wondered. You then estimated the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept and slope of each
            equation that was graphed.</item>
        </list></item>
        <item>2.2.2: Writing Systems of Equations from Tables
        <list id="list-00004">
          <item>In this activity, you created a table of values for a given situation, then wrote a
            system of equations from two tables of values.</item>
          <item>2.2.2: Self Check</item>
          <item>2.2.2: Additional Resources</item>
        </list></item>
        <item>2.2.3: Graphs of Systems of Equation
        <list id="list-00005">
          <item>In this activity, you wrote a system of equations from a graph, then worked
            backward to graph a system of equations by hand given the equations.</item>
          <item>2.2.3: Self Check</item>
          <item>2.2.3: Additional Resources</item>
        </list></item>
        <item>2.2.4: Systems of Equations in the Real-World
        <list id="list-00006">
          <item>In this activity, you wrote a system of equations for a given situation, then
            graphed the system and estimated the solution from the graph.</item>
        </list></item>
      </list>
      <para id="para-00003">After these activities, you completed the following <emphasis>practice</emphasis>:</para>
      <list id="list-00007">
        <item>2.2.5: Practice</item>
      </list>
      <section class="checking-in" id="note-00001" data-platform-hidden="assignable">
        <title>Checking In</title>
        <exercise id="e947d4a4-28d1-427e-ad5b-f6987098498e" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00001">
            <para id="para-00004">On a scale of 1 to 5, how confident do you feel about the learning goals of this lesson?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00001">
            <para id="para-00005">Nice reflection! You learn more when you take the time to reflect on your thinking.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
    </section>
  </content>
